        "1": {
          "ARC-REV-01": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Views.fs",
                "line": 335,
                "quote": "let owed = library.Fines |> List.map (fun fine -> fine.Member) |> List.distinct |> List.sumBy (fun memberId -> Accounts.owed memberId library)"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 195,
                "quote": "Error(InvalidInput $\"{path} already exists\")"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The per-member debt rule (fines less payments) stays in Tier 2: the Tier 3 projection calls Accounts.owed and does not recompute it. But the library-wide 'total all members owe' is derived in Tier 3. The view also decides locally which members count as owing (only members that appear in Fines). That is a small local special case of a Tier 2 rule, and it does not contradict it. Restore, backup-info and the backup-refusal check are use-case coordination. No lending legality rule moves into Tier 3 or 4. The CLI only renders views.",
            "score": 1
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Host/Cli/CommandLine.fs",
                "line": 195,
                "quote": "| Ok [ \"backup\"; path ] -> UseCases.backup ports path |> render showBackup"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 176,
                "quote": "ports.Archive.Load path"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "All new I/O goes through existing ports (Archive.Load/Save, Files.ReadLines, Store.Load/Save). The change also removes an existing violation: the CLI used to call JsonFileStore.create directly. No effect reaches Tier 1/2, and there is no new clock or console use. Minor note: loadBackup uses a catch-all 'with _ -> None' in Tier 3 (ARC-HEU-01 style). This folds read failures into 'no backup' but does not bypass a port.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Views.fs",
                "line": 326,
                "quote": "let summary (library: Library) : LibrarySummaryView ="
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The library summary is defined once (Views.summary) and used by backup, restore and backup-info. The CLI's showSummary renders it once. Owed amounts come from the Tier 2 Accounts.owed function, and money formatting uses the existing Views.money helper. No literal or predicate is copied.",
            "score": 2
          }
        },
        "2": {
          "ARC-REV-01": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Catalog.fs",
                "line": 16,
                "quote": "let restoreMember memberId (backup: Library) (library: Library) : Result<Library * Member * Fine list * Payment list, LendingError> ="
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "Tier 2 (Catalog.restoreMember) decides everything about restoring a member. That covers whether the backup holds the member, the duplicate-member guard (ensure ... DuplicateMember), which fines and payments come back, and that loans, holds and reminders stay behind. Tier 3 only loads the backup, calls Catalog.restoreMember inside commit and projects a view. The CLI only renders it.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 212,
                "quote": "commit ports (fun _ library -> Catalog.restoreMember (MemberId memberId) backup library"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The Tier 2 function is pure: it takes the backup Library as a value. Tier 3 reads the backup through the existing Archive port (loadBackup) and saves through the existing commit/Store path. The CLI calls only the use case. No new effect reaches Tier 1/2, and nothing in Tier 4 calls Tier 2.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Catalog.fs",
                "line": 23,
                "quote": "do! ensure (not (library.Members.ContainsKey memberId)) (DuplicateMember memberId)"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The 'member already exists' refusal reuses the existing DuplicateMember error, which addMember also uses, so the message comes from one place. 'No backup' reuses the existing noBackup helper. The rule for which fines and payments belong to the member is defined once, in Tier 2, and the view only counts what Tier 2 returns.",
            "score": 2
          }
